{
    "background_story": "Dutton was a renowned musicologist who spent his life studying the works of Mozart. However, his true passion project was uncovering the lost compositions of Maria Anna Mozart, the sister of the famous composer. Dutton became obsessed with the idea that Maria, a talented musician in her own right, had written music that was lost to the ages. After years of searching, he finally stumbled upon an old manuscript in a dusty archive, which he believed to be Maria's long-lost symphony. Dutton dedicated himself to authenticating and performing the piece, which he named 'Maria's Echo'. The symphony premiered to critical acclaim, and Dutton's work brought Maria's genius to the forefront, earning him international recognition and cementing his legacy as a champion of forgotten musical treasures.",
